+/* DWM composes a window that draws only through DirectComposition (WS_EX_NOREDIRECTIONBITMAP)
+ * with per-pixel alpha over whatever lies behind it. An owned popup of that kind (WinUI 3's
+ * PopupWindowSiteBridge: ComboBox drop-downs, flyouts) shows the owner through its transparent
+ * parts and around its rounded corners, so it is presented as a layered window here. The main
+ * window keeps the opaque swapchain path: it is fully painted and a CPU read-back would cost
+ * too much at its size. HACK: setting WS_EX_LAYERED on the application's window ourselves. */
+static BOOL target_wants_alpha(HWND hwnd)
